Description: Use a lighter release profile for heavy build-time crates
 diesel and the -sys crates dominate peak memory during a release build.
 Give them opt-level=0 and lto=false so the overall build fits on small
 ARM boards, while the main workspace keeps LTO.
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: Michales Michaloudes <korgie@gmail.com>
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -1,3 +1,8 @@
+# Per-package release profile overrides to reduce peak memory during build.
+# These do not affect the shipped binary's behavior.
+
+[profile.release.package.diesel]
+opt-level = 0
+codegen-units = 32
+lto = false
+
